# Golden SER0 transcript for the clicky boot smoke (tests/scripts/clicky_smoke.py).
#
# One line per `core: ` status line the firmware emits between reset and
# the idle task, in order, and NOTHING else may appear between them. The
# run is stopped the moment the last line arrives, so this is the whole
# transcript, not a prefix — a doubled line (the COP-park regression, where
# both cores raced through kernel_main) or a missing one fails the diff.
#
# Only BOOT MILESTONES belong here. A field that legitimately differs
# between the emulator and the device, or between runs, is written as
# <hex32> and matched as any eight hex digits:
#   - PROCESSOR_ID reads 0x55 on silicon and 0x55555555 in clicky (its
#     4G quirk; see 01-soc-pp5022.md "Dual core"). crt0.S compares only
#     the low byte, so both are the CPU.
#   - cpu freq reads the post-PLL clock. clicky never sets the PLL lock
#     bit, so the bounded lock poll gives up and the clock stays at the
#     24 MHz boot crystal there; the device reports 30 MHz.
# Nothing in this file is a timing number. Do not add one.
#
# The last two lines are the ones that make this more than a "did C run"
# check: `sched init` proves kernel_main survived timer_init + the IRQ
# unmask, and `idle task entered` is printed FROM the idle task, which is
# only reached through switch_context + task_trampoline in kernel/switch.S
# — the first restore of a hand-built initial frame, on a hand-carved
# stack. That asm had no automated coverage of any kind before this file.
#
# To regenerate after a DELIBERATE change to the boot log: run the smoke
# locally (see the script's docstring), copy the `core: ` lines from its
# transcript, and re-apply the <hex32> masks above. Then explain the change
# in the commit that carries it.
core: kernel alive (iPod 5G/5.5G, PP5022)
core: uart self-test 1234ABCD
core: PROCESSOR_ID <hex32>
core: clock init -> 30 MHz
core: cpu freq <hex32>
core: cache init
core: timer init @ 100 Hz, enabling IRQs
core: lcd bcm NOT powered, skipping disk + UI
core: sched init (idle fallback)
core: idle task entered
